Number of spans: the default batch queue holds 2048 spans. A large account with many records could exceed that, and spans past the limit are dropped. If that happens, raise max_queue_size in init_tracer.
AWS SDK spans: the AWS SDK emits its own tracing spans. The layer from step 2 picks them up automatically, so each describe_load_balancers request appears as a child span. Filter them out with EnvFilter if they are too noisy.
Trace IDs on log records: messages sent through service_log probably won't carry the trace ID, because a tracing span doesn't set the current OTel context automatically. If you want to jump from a Loki log line to its trace, replace service_log with opentelemetry-appender-tracing later. I'd treat that as a separate change


